    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d503">

                <pb facs="0641" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg529"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.515/398a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Department of State to
                        the Chinese Legation</hi><anchor n="35"
                        xml:id="d503-f1"/></head>
                <p>Up to the present time the American Government, although it has made informally
                    suggestions toward that end, has not received from the Chinese Government data
                    indicating in any detail and with any particular exactness the character and the
                    extent of the adverse effects which the silver purchasing program of the United
                    States is said to be causing in China.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1935-01-26">January 26,
                            1935</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d503-f1" n="35" type="source" xml:id="d503-f1-content">
                <p>Handed to the Chinese Minister by the Chief of the Division of Far Eastern
                    Affairs, January 26.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
